1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,120
Last time, we learned to make every number from zero to nine.

2
00:00:04,920 --> 00:00:08,100
Today, we're going to put two numbers together.

3
00:00:08,840 --> 00:00:12,500
When we put two numbers together, that's called adding.

4
00:00:13,260 --> 00:00:16,080
And the abacus makes adding really easy.

5
00:00:17,260 --> 00:00:20,500
Adding on the abacus means moving more beads to the beam.

6
00:00:21,500 --> 00:00:23,600
First, make your starting number.

7
00:00:24,200 --> 00:00:27,900
Then, push up as many more beads as you want to add.

8
00:00:28,480 --> 00:00:32,040
When you stop, the rod is already showing the answer.

9
00:00:33,020 --> 00:00:35,540
Let's try one plus two together.

10
00:00:36,300 --> 00:00:39,860
To make one, push one lower bead up to the beam.

11
00:00:40,660 --> 00:00:42,080
The rod is showing one.

12
00:00:42,920 --> 00:00:47,100
Now, add two by pushing two more lower beads up.

13
00:00:48,000 --> 00:00:49,200
Count them as they go up.

14
00:00:49,960 --> 00:00:51,540
One, two.

15
00:00:52,300 --> 00:00:54,720
Three lower beads are touching the beam.

16
00:00:55,360 --> 00:00:57,180
So, one plus two is three.

17
00:00:58,040 --> 00:01:00,480
Now, let's try two plus two.

18
00:01:00,960 --> 00:01:04,840
To make two, push two lower beads up to the beam.

19
00:01:05,620 --> 00:01:09,580
Now, add two more by pushing two more lower beads up.

20
00:01:10,500 --> 00:01:13,040
All four lower beads are touching the beam.

21
00:01:13,780 --> 00:01:15,620
So, two plus two is four.

22
00:01:16,980 --> 00:01:19,960
Every lower bead you push up adds one more.

23
00:01:20,580 --> 00:01:23,360
But each rod only has four lower beads.

24
00:01:24,020 --> 00:01:28,820
So, the lower beads can only make one, two, three or four.

25
00:01:29,720 --> 00:01:33,980
When we want to add five, we use the upper bead instead.

26
00:01:34,660 --> 00:01:37,300
Start with all the beads away from the beam.

27
00:01:37,820 --> 00:01:39,340
So, the rod is showing zero.

28
00:01:40,300 --> 00:01:43,760
Now, push the upper bead down until it touches the beam.

29
00:01:44,600 --> 00:01:46,200
The rod is showing five.

30
00:01:47,140 --> 00:01:50,660
One single bead gave us five in one move.

31
00:01:51,760 --> 00:01:54,320
Now, let's try five plus one.

32
00:01:55,000 --> 00:01:58,480
First, make five by pushing the upper bead down.

33
00:01:59,400 --> 00:02:02,820
Then, add one by pushing one lower bead up.

34
00:02:03,740 --> 00:02:07,820
The upper bead is worth five and the lower bead is worth one.

35
00:02:08,420 --> 00:02:10,420
So, five plus one is six.

36
00:02:12,020 --> 00:02:13,980
Let's try five plus four.

37
00:02:14,780 --> 00:02:17,740
Make five again by pushing the upper bead down.

38
00:02:18,500 --> 00:02:21,520
Now, push all four lower beads up to the beam.

39
00:02:22,420 --> 00:02:25,020
Five and four more makes nine.

40
00:02:26,200 --> 00:02:30,200
This works when you start from any number, not only five.

41
00:02:31,000 --> 00:02:32,160
Let's start from six.

42
00:02:33,140 --> 00:02:36,640
To make six, push the upper bead down for five.

43
00:02:37,320 --> 00:02:39,980
Then, push one lower bead up for one.

44
00:02:40,720 --> 00:02:42,180
The rod is showing six.

45
00:02:43,300 --> 00:02:47,200
Now, add three by pushing three more lower beads up.

46
00:02:47,740 --> 00:02:49,820
Six plus three is nine.

47
00:02:50,820 --> 00:02:52,340
Let's do one more.

48
00:02:52,920 --> 00:02:54,020
Start with seven.

49
00:02:54,860 --> 00:02:57,660
To make seven, push the upper bead down.

50
00:02:58,240 --> 00:03:00,280
Then, push two lower beads up.

51
00:03:01,300 --> 00:03:04,760
Now, add one by pushing one more lower bead up.

52
00:03:05,660 --> 00:03:07,440
Seven plus one is eight.

53
00:03:08,640 --> 00:03:09,880
Now, it's your turn.

54
00:03:10,540 --> 00:03:13,400
Try five plus two on your own abacus.

55
00:03:14,240 --> 00:03:16,560
Push the upper bead down to make five.

56
00:03:16,560 --> 00:03:19,160
Then, push two lower beads up.

57
00:03:19,780 --> 00:03:21,380
The rod is showing seven.

58
00:03:22,120 --> 00:03:24,020
So, five plus two is seven.

59
00:03:24,820 --> 00:03:25,420
Great job.

60
00:03:26,800 --> 00:03:28,680
Here's one last thing to notice.

61
00:03:29,620 --> 00:03:30,960
Make one on your rod.

62
00:03:31,860 --> 00:03:33,480
Now, try to add four more.

63
00:03:34,300 --> 00:03:36,680
There are only three lower beads left.

64
00:03:37,340 --> 00:03:38,580
There isn't enough room.

65
00:03:39,520 --> 00:03:41,760
There's a clever trick for moments like this.

66
00:03:42,220 --> 00:03:43,940
And we'll learn it very soon.

67
00:03:45,040 --> 00:03:49,060
Now, try adding some small numbers on your own abacus.

68
00:03:49,740 --> 00:03:53,460
If you enjoyed this video, please like and subscribe for more.

69
00:03:54,200 --> 00:03:58,160
Search for abacus kids on the Apple App Store or Google Play.

70
00:03:58,840 --> 00:03:59,760
Download it free.

71
00:04:00,740 --> 00:04:05,800
See you in the next video, where we'll add much bigger numbers on the abacus.
